~ start
Prime Minister Terborg: Mr President, breakfast in the Netherlands is a matter of efficiency. Shall we say our sins quickly and eat our cheese in peace?
- Raise the Rotterdam port rules => port
- Raise the sea wall and flood funds => sea
- Raise the farm nitrogen cuts => nitrogen
~ port
Prime Minister Terborg: Rotterdam is Europe's front door, and it wishes the neighbours would stop leaving muddy boots on the mat.
- Offer a shared customs window => customs
- Offer to share the Le Havre berths => berths
~ customs
Prime Minister Terborg: A shared customs window. Smugglers will hate it. Accountants will adore it.
=> END
~ berths
Prime Minister Terborg: Berths at Le Havre, yes. We are friendly competitors, and the competition has the better lunch.
=> END
~ sea
Prime Minister Terborg: The sea is always patient, and so are we. But patience is expensive, and I would rather share the cost.
- Offer French engineers for the delta works => delta
- Offer a joint resilience fund => resilience
~ delta
Prime Minister Terborg: French engineers, on Dutch dikes. The water will not know the difference, and neither will the invoices.
=> END
~ resilience
Prime Minister Terborg: A resilience fund. I am told it is the word of the decade. Let us see whether it holds water.
=> END
~ nitrogen
Prime Minister Terborg: The farmers parked their tractors on the motorway for a week, and I have not been popular since.
- Sympathise with the farmers => farmers
- Back the nitrogen cuts => cuts
~ farmers
Prime Minister Terborg: Kind of you. My farmers will remember, and so will my environment minister, with less warmth.
=> END
~ cuts
Prime Minister Terborg: Brave. They will call you a bureaucrat at home, but then so will they call me.
=> END
